      "writtenOn": "2020-08-18T09:14:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I\u0027ll fix this:\n\nMost references I have found indicate that High-Z pull-up and pull-down are near identical, sweetberry results didn\u0027t show any difference. (GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_PULL_UP). I picked PULL_UP because it was more common in the EC codebase.\n\nAn unconnected GPIO\u0027s consumption comes from 2 areas mostly: We want to avoid current flowing though the pull-up or pull-down resistors and avoid the input circuit from toggling or otherwise left floating between high and low. Enabling either direction achieves that goal because once the input is at a given voltage, current stops flowing though the pull resistor apart from the internal leakage.",
      "parentUuid": "a8aa7d2f_08c28efb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
