        "id": 1347380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-18T09:14:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This concerns me, I don\u0027t know enough about this chip to identify if this is an issue, it looks like it expects to be in an operating mode, \u0027Power switch logic mode for ultra-low power\u0027 that doesn\u0027t have the GPIO\u0027s 84 or 85 configured, I don\u0027t see GPIO84, the VSBY configured on the layouts so I\u0027m assuming it\u0027s floating NC as well:\n\nI attempted to disable that pin but found that it is configured based on the NPCX_PSL_MODE_SUPPORT status which appears to be enabled due to our chip variant but doesn\u0027t appear to be used.\n\n\nFrom config_chip-npcx7.h:\n\n#if defined(CHIP_VARIANT_NPCX7M6F) || defined(CHIP_VARIANT_NPCX7M6FB) || \\\n\tdefined(CHIP_VARIANT_NPCX7M6FC) || defined(CHIP_VARIANT_NPCX7M7WB) || \\\n\tdefined(CHIP_VARIANT_NPCX7M7WC)\n#define NPCX_INT_FLASH_SUPPORT /* Internal flash support */\n#define NPCX_PSL_MODE_SUPPORT /* Power switch logic mode for ultra-low power */\n#define NPCX_EXT32K_OSC_SUPPORT /* External 32KHz crytal osc. input support */\n#endif\n\nFrom gpio_chip-npcx7.h\"\n\n#ifndef NPCX_PSL_MODE_SUPPORT\n#define NPCX_WUI_GPIO_8_4 WUI(0, MIWU_GROUP_1, 4) /* Used as VSBY in PSL */\n#define NPCX_WUI_GPIO_8_5 WUI(0, MIWU_GROUP_1, 5) /* Used as PSL_OUT in PSL */\n#endif",
      "parentUuid": "4b1040de_a0f124fc",
